WEBVTT

00:16.720 --> 00:18.640
Something more rhythmic.

00:18.810 --> 00:20.390
TIMETABLE

00:20.100 --> 00:21.140
Perfect!

00:22.060 --> 00:25.100
A faster tempo, perhaps.

00:28.150 --> 00:28.900
Not a bad idea…

00:30.980 --> 00:32.610
<i>Percussion that sets the tone,</i>

00:33.190 --> 00:36.820
<i>a stimulating melody and flowing lyrics.</i>

00:42.330 --> 00:46.170
<i>That moment when you realize that everything sounds perfect.</i>

00:46.920 --> 00:49.790
<i>That feeling of euphoria that sends you over the moon.</i>

00:54.840 --> 00:56.050
Midnight already.

00:59.470 --> 01:03.020
What? Pull yourself together!

01:03.180 --> 01:06.390
You've got to study, damn it! Study!

01:08.900 --> 01:11.650
Well, it's not enough to stupidly superimpose them.

01:13.030 --> 01:17.660
Maybe I should try to tone down the intensity.

01:32.210 --> 01:33.250
Come on, study!

03:04.600 --> 03:09.270
MINDLESS QUESTION-ANSWER

03:13.980 --> 03:15.070
You've got to be kidding me!

03:16.940 --> 03:18.400
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

03:19.570 --> 03:22.990
<i>The pigeon was on the rhythm…</i>

03:24.370 --> 03:25.450
Concentrate!

03:26.660 --> 03:28.830
<i>I'm at the same point as yesterday.</i>

03:29.000 --> 03:32.000
<i>Yeah, I lost a whole day.</i>

03:34.460 --> 03:35.290
<i>Guitar.</i>

03:35.460 --> 03:38.840
<i>I wonder if she's got a dry one.</i>

03:41.630 --> 03:42.840
Hi, it's me.

03:43.680 --> 03:45.470
Hi, Nina!

03:46.050 --> 03:47.310
Have you eaten yet?

03:47.720 --> 03:48.470
No, I haven't.

03:48.640 --> 03:51.600
Would you like a meat bun? They're generous!

03:53.480 --> 03:55.360
Pay your manners!

03:55.520 --> 03:57.730
You're a real bourge.

03:58.110 --> 03:59.730
What kind of sauce is that?

04:00.030 --> 04:01.610
I promise, it tastes better with it.

04:02.530 --> 04:03.610
In fact, a friend of mine

04:03.780 --> 04:06.830
a friend of mine gave me some unsold merchandise from her job.

04:06.990 --> 04:07.950
So good.

04:10.370 --> 04:11.120
You like it?

04:11.710 --> 04:13.620
Yes, it's too good.

04:14.000 --> 04:16.040
It's great. Glad to hear it.

04:20.010 --> 04:22.920
So, what about this song? Have you finished the composition?

04:23.130 --> 04:25.930
You can't do it in two shakes, you know.

04:26.140 --> 04:28.350
Then why did you ask us here?

04:28.510 --> 04:30.770
It's a bit of a step for me.

04:31.140 --> 04:34.060
I just thought we needed to agree.

04:34.310 --> 04:38.150
Like, about our style. What suits us best?

04:38.690 --> 04:41.780
Well, as long as I can play the drums…

04:42.940 --> 04:43.780
What do you think?

04:44.280 --> 04:45.950
It's so good!

04:54.330 --> 04:58.500
I showed you this app, what, a week ago?

04:58.670 --> 05:01.840
And you're already doing so well! Classy!

05:02.010 --> 05:04.090
It's just that… Momoka told me

05:04.260 --> 05:07.590
that I could compose without having studied music theory.

05:07.760 --> 05:08.930
So I gave it a try.

05:09.260 --> 05:12.680
Still, for the result to be this accomplished,

05:13.220 --> 05:15.770
you must have spent at least 8 hours a day on it.

05:20.860 --> 05:21.780
Where are you off to?

05:22.530 --> 05:23.490
Home.

05:24.610 --> 05:27.610
I've got to work! Work some more!

05:28.410 --> 05:29.280
Gaulée.

05:30.450 --> 05:33.700
You promised me this wouldn't interfere with my studies!

05:33.870 --> 05:35.830
This is your fault!

05:36.000 --> 05:37.210
You're the one at fault.

05:37.670 --> 05:38.830
Yeah, I know.

05:39.130 --> 05:41.250
Don't throw accusations around, then.

05:42.960 --> 05:43.840
It's just…

05:44.010 --> 05:45.340
Okay, fine.

05:45.510 --> 05:49.680
I shouldn't have shown you that app. I'll just uninstall it…

05:49.840 --> 05:51.510
All right, forget it.

05:51.680 --> 05:52.760
What, in the end?

05:52.970 --> 05:54.180
It's all my fault.

05:54.350 --> 05:58.980
I work on my side, and you manage the group. Easy, isn't it?

05:59.230 --> 06:00.520
Who are you talking to?

06:01.650 --> 06:02.900
Who do you think I'm talking to?

06:03.070 --> 06:04.650
See you at pro week.

06:07.360 --> 06:10.280
Honestly, you have to follow it. An enigma on legs.

06:11.240 --> 06:12.780
Well, I won't stay long either.

06:13.870 --> 06:15.950
Just a minute! There's the bun armor.

06:16.120 --> 06:18.040
Knock yourself out. Later!

06:21.750 --> 06:22.790
Hey, Nina!

06:24.670 --> 06:25.960
Shall we drive together?

06:27.510 --> 06:28.430
If you like.

06:29.840 --> 06:33.560
Still, it takes a lot to write a song on your own.

06:33.850 --> 06:35.560
Clearly, I couldn't have done it.

06:36.770 --> 06:40.150
You bet I couldn't. I cobbled something together from information here and there.

06:41.350 --> 06:44.940
Okay, but I wouldn't have been able to write lyrics.

06:46.030 --> 06:47.440
If you say so.

06:47.610 --> 06:48.110
That's right.

06:54.240 --> 06:57.450
I'm sorry, but I've got to run to the mini-mart.

06:58.870 --> 06:59.710
Then let's go.

07:00.080 --> 07:01.290
No. I mean…

07:01.540 --> 07:04.880
Actually, I was planning on walking home.

07:05.920 --> 07:06.670
Well, suit yourself.

07:07.760 --> 07:08.380
I'll see you soon.

07:23.270 --> 07:24.610
Subaru too.

07:26.020 --> 07:29.240
Can't you manage… I mean, can't you go?

07:29.610 --> 07:32.860
I can't, I'm working. You don't have the time?

07:33.110 --> 07:35.200
That's not what I said, but here goes…

07:35.370 --> 07:37.830
Look, you can wait until after school.

07:37.990 --> 07:39.250
It's not that complicated.

07:39.540 --> 07:40.580
For the buns.

07:46.210 --> 07:47.750
This place is famous.

07:48.090 --> 07:48.840
Check it out.

07:49.090 --> 07:50.170
Country girl spotted.

07:52.800 --> 07:53.760
Well, which way is it?

07:54.220 --> 07:55.430
Let's see…

07:56.300 --> 07:57.640
Well…

07:58.350 --> 07:59.140
There, I guess.

07:59.770 --> 08:00.890
Or not, as it turns out.

08:06.440 --> 08:07.520
Ah, there it is!

08:15.200 --> 08:18.080
Is anybody home?

08:19.700 --> 08:21.290
Can I help you?

08:25.040 --> 08:26.080
Yes!

08:26.250 --> 08:28.840
Is Awa around?

08:29.000 --> 08:30.050
Awa?

08:30.300 --> 08:31.670
You mean Subaru!

08:33.090 --> 08:34.050
Over here, Subaru!

08:34.430 --> 08:36.930
Yes, we're not changing the room.

08:38.850 --> 08:39.930
Nina!

08:40.270 --> 08:41.310
Why are you here?

08:42.520 --> 08:44.190
Wasn't it hard to find?

08:44.350 --> 08:47.190
I could have come to meet you, you know.

08:47.560 --> 08:49.150
Sorry I took so long.

08:49.440 --> 08:50.280
Here you go.

08:51.650 --> 08:52.860
My savior!

08:53.490 --> 08:55.110
Did you forget your cell phone?

08:55.280 --> 08:55.780
Yeah, I did.

08:56.700 --> 08:57.870
She's such a spaz.

08:58.530 --> 08:59.950
Everyone's waiting for you.

09:00.370 --> 09:02.120
- ALL RIGHT, THEN.
- See you.

09:02.290 --> 09:03.750
Yeah, see you in a bit.

09:03.910 --> 09:06.920
You have a moment, don't you? How about grabbing a bite to eat?

09:07.080 --> 09:08.000
My treat.

09:09.380 --> 09:12.920
Sorry, I have to work, you understand…

09:13.550 --> 09:15.430
Are you free this weekend?

09:15.590 --> 09:16.590
Like Sunday?

09:17.640 --> 09:21.720
Honestly, you don't have to, you know. It's a small favor.

09:21.930 --> 09:23.520
Well, I'll leave you to it.

09:26.100 --> 09:27.350
Do you want me to go?

09:29.650 --> 09:32.570
I'm talking about the band. I'm embarrassing you, aren't I?

09:33.610 --> 09:37.700
I'm not stupid, you know. I can see you've been avoiding me.

09:38.410 --> 09:39.490
Well, uh…

09:39.660 --> 09:42.200
I'm not trying to get in your way.

09:42.540 --> 09:44.080
There are other groups.

09:44.450 --> 09:48.040
Wait, you're not in it. I'm telling you, you're wrong.

09:48.210 --> 09:49.460
It's just that…

09:54.300 --> 09:55.300
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

09:58.090 --> 09:59.090
You're sure, right?

09:59.680 --> 10:03.430
Yeah, don't worry. I can always study later.

10:03.600 --> 10:05.310
Or another day, after all.

10:05.480 --> 10:07.270
No, I wanted to talk about myself.

10:08.770 --> 10:11.900
I started playing music in high school.

10:12.070 --> 10:14.400
I'm far from an expert.

10:14.940 --> 10:18.240
Generally speaking, the members of a band are pretty tight,

10:18.450 --> 10:20.160
because they're working together.

10:20.700 --> 10:24.080
So it's hard to get past disagreements.

10:24.790 --> 10:29.330
Refusing to get to the bottom of things only feeds misunderstanding.

10:30.330 --> 10:34.130
If you don't like something, you'd better say it loud and clear.

10:34.420 --> 10:36.670
I've got nothing against you, you know.

10:37.550 --> 10:39.180
It's all my fault.

10:39.680 --> 10:41.470
The same old story.

10:42.260 --> 10:44.100
People usually hate me.

10:45.390 --> 10:47.850
No, concentrate! Come on, focus!

10:48.020 --> 10:50.270
I'm used to standing back.

10:50.440 --> 10:53.480
I'm afraid people will force themselves to take a step towards me.

10:53.650 --> 10:55.610
Why, don't you like it?

10:56.030 --> 10:57.240
No, it's not that.

10:57.400 --> 11:00.780
But I don't know, when someone's being friendly with me,

11:00.950 --> 11:04.490
I can't help feeling that it's going to turn ugly

11:04.830 --> 11:07.080
after a while.

11:07.620 --> 11:08.960
The headaches…

11:09.120 --> 11:11.960
And I suppose that's why you dropped out of high school?

11:12.460 --> 11:14.170
No, nothing like that.

11:14.420 --> 11:17.340
Wait a minute, wait a minute. She spilled the beans?

11:18.010 --> 11:18.800
Bull's-eye.

11:19.800 --> 11:22.470
You like playing the good prince, don't you?

11:23.930 --> 11:24.850
All right, that's enough.

11:25.760 --> 11:27.470
You're totally wrong about me.

11:27.970 --> 11:31.350
Yeah, I may be taking a theater class,

11:31.520 --> 11:34.230
but I'll have you know that doesn't lead to a degree.

11:34.610 --> 11:36.230
We're in the same situation.

11:36.610 --> 11:38.900
Maybe, but you want to be an actress.

11:39.110 --> 11:41.990
That means you're following a dream!

11:42.360 --> 11:44.620
At least you've got something to say to other people!

11:45.160 --> 11:47.240
And that's where you're wrong.

11:49.790 --> 11:50.910
Do you know her?

11:51.920 --> 11:53.750
Her face looks familiar.

11:54.250 --> 11:57.750
<i>Granny's Investigations</i>.
Rebroadcast every noon.

11:59.210 --> 12:01.170
That woman is my grandmother.

12:01.420 --> 12:01.930
You're kidding.

12:02.130 --> 12:06.050
It's a pain in the ass, you have no idea. Madame demands that I follow in her footsteps.

12:06.220 --> 12:09.770
She's arranged to send me to that school.

12:10.350 --> 12:12.520
Don't you want to be an actress?

12:12.770 --> 12:14.560
Not really, to be honest.

12:15.190 --> 12:17.980
And yet, you continue to follow this curriculum…

12:18.150 --> 12:20.490
Yeah, and it fuels my self-hatred.

12:22.280 --> 12:24.700
It's stupid to get so worked up over something you don't want.

12:25.030 --> 12:27.620
But the people around me don't care.

12:27.780 --> 12:32.080
Everyone thinks I'm just trying to carry on the family tradition.

12:32.460 --> 12:33.670
And why music?

12:33.960 --> 12:36.130
It's my way of gently protesting.

12:36.380 --> 12:40.170
I didn't want to have to go to drama club, you see.

12:40.590 --> 12:43.680
I joined a band because I liked the idea.

12:43.840 --> 12:45.680
I had a blast.

12:46.300 --> 12:48.680
And all in the greatest secrecy.

12:49.100 --> 12:50.680
Your grandmother doesn't know?

12:50.850 --> 12:52.270
Well, she'd have to.

12:52.890 --> 12:54.640
By the way, have you seen the statue of Hachiko?

12:54.980 --> 12:56.810
We're going to look like country girls.

12:56.980 --> 12:59.020
So what if we are? You are one, after all.

12:59.440 --> 13:01.570
Come on, that's for listening to me.

13:03.280 --> 13:05.990
We're friends, you won't get rid of me again!

13:07.780 --> 13:09.200
<i>Girls Band Cry.</i>

13:10.080 --> 13:12.370
SUNDAY NOON

13:10.740 --> 13:11.950
A street show?

13:12.750 --> 13:15.080
Yeah, that would be a good start.

13:15.250 --> 13:17.880
I've already booked a slot this weekend.

13:19.170 --> 13:22.920
Shouldn't we start by recording a song?

13:23.510 --> 13:25.090
That's still on the agenda.

13:25.300 --> 13:28.760
But something tells me we've got to get going fast,

13:29.140 --> 13:31.560
- especially with our line-up.
- Concert, then.

13:31.850 --> 13:34.230
I mean, look at your picture.

13:34.390 --> 13:38.900
You've got the right mix of desperation and frustration.

13:39.060 --> 13:40.770
- You're not nice.
- Definitely.

13:41.150 --> 13:44.650
But that's exactly why I turned to you two.

13:44.990 --> 13:46.320
to the two of you.

13:47.200 --> 13:50.120
- What do you think, Nina?
- I don't know, but okay.

13:50.450 --> 13:52.540
Maybe there's some truth in that.

13:52.910 --> 13:55.830
I mean, are you sure we can do without a bass player?

13:56.210 --> 13:58.040
You don't play any instruments, do you?

13:58.380 --> 14:01.710
Relax, it's an amateur thing. We'll manage.

14:01.920 --> 14:03.670
Besides, we're equipped.

14:04.380 --> 14:05.170
What's a looper?

14:05.420 --> 14:06.470
A looper.

14:07.130 --> 14:09.300
To record a musical loop.

14:16.940 --> 14:17.520
Get it?

14:19.020 --> 14:20.150
Too well.

14:20.520 --> 14:23.730
Wait a minute, I hit it on time.

14:24.230 --> 14:26.320
Are we going to perform in front of people?

14:26.650 --> 14:30.950
What do you think? Besides, you've already seen me perform.

14:34.450 --> 14:36.200
- Where are you off to?
- Home.

14:37.660 --> 14:39.000
Stop your capriciousness.

14:39.170 --> 14:41.210
Get your hands off me! That wasn't the plan!

14:41.630 --> 14:44.420
Pull yourself together. You sang at the station!

14:44.590 --> 14:45.760
It's all the same.

14:45.920 --> 14:48.050
Easier said than done.

14:48.220 --> 14:50.470
It's a leap into the unknown for me!

14:50.800 --> 14:53.970
I'll be there to make up for it if anything goes wrong.

14:54.470 --> 14:56.850
Madame only has to sing, if she's so good!

14:57.020 --> 14:58.850
You've got a much better voice.

14:59.020 --> 15:00.480
And you'll be the guitarist?

15:00.810 --> 15:02.440
No, and you know it.

15:02.610 --> 15:06.230
I told you I wanted you behind the mike.

15:06.480 --> 15:07.570
But why?

15:08.320 --> 15:10.990
You'll understand when you sing. Just trust me on this.

15:16.160 --> 15:17.040
I'll leave you to it.

15:17.290 --> 15:19.660
So, you're quitting the band?

15:20.460 --> 15:22.500
Yes, exactly. Thank you and Godspeed!

15:25.920 --> 15:26.710
But…

15:27.880 --> 15:28.670
Don't worry.

15:38.600 --> 15:41.230
You've got a lot of nerve backing us into a corner!

15:41.730 --> 15:42.900
You're not making any sense.

15:43.060 --> 15:45.230
- Put yourself in my shoes…
- Stop freaking out.

15:45.860 --> 15:49.320
Whether it goes wrong or not, whether you fail or not,

15:49.490 --> 15:51.700
you're gonna have regrets in the end.

15:51.860 --> 15:53.370
It's in your personality.

15:53.740 --> 15:55.700
- You're overreacting…
- It's the truth.

15:55.870 --> 15:57.490
Believe me, you've got everything to gain,

15:57.660 --> 16:01.000
by getting out there and singing your heart out.

16:01.370 --> 16:02.170
Am I wrong?

16:03.830 --> 16:05.500
Here, admit defeat.

16:05.670 --> 16:06.920
I didn't ring your bell!

16:07.250 --> 16:09.260
Pour your anger into the music.

16:09.960 --> 16:11.720
That's what's eating you up inside.

16:15.850 --> 16:17.680
They've got some nice gear!

16:18.060 --> 16:21.020
Plus, it's really cheap to rent.

16:23.270 --> 16:24.440
Let's test it out.

16:34.780 --> 16:36.240
Yeah, that'll do the trick.

16:36.410 --> 16:39.040
Nina, do you have the lyrics of the song in mind?

16:39.200 --> 16:42.540
I tried to fit in what you'd done, too.

16:42.710 --> 16:43.330
Yes.

16:43.670 --> 16:45.420
Let's get started, then.

16:46.380 --> 16:48.590
Why do you think we came?

16:49.000 --> 16:50.840
You caught me off guard!

16:51.090 --> 16:53.470
Stop freaking out, I'm telling you.

16:53.630 --> 16:56.510
It's only a rehearsal, it's bound to be bad.

16:57.220 --> 16:58.930
A real debacle.

16:59.260 --> 16:59.930
Catch.

17:17.780 --> 17:18.660
Breathe in.

17:37.720 --> 17:38.930
<i>One, two, three, four.</i>

17:51.860 --> 17:52.780
How's that sound?

17:56.570 --> 17:59.320
It gave me the shivers.

17:59.740 --> 18:01.530
Yeah, goosebumps!

18:01.870 --> 18:02.870
There you go.

18:04.080 --> 18:06.460
You've fallen right into Momoka's trap.

18:06.620 --> 18:09.330
Once you've tasted it, there's no turning back.

18:10.500 --> 18:12.340
What's that supposed to mean?

18:12.800 --> 18:13.920
Human beings

18:14.090 --> 18:17.590
can't help but move to the rhythm of a sound.

18:17.800 --> 18:20.720
Dance and music go hand in hand, it's in our DNA.

18:20.890 --> 18:21.430
Isn't it?

18:21.720 --> 18:22.350
Yes, it is.

18:23.350 --> 18:24.520
What's the matter?

18:24.680 --> 18:27.770
Nothing, I just thought you'd have one hell of a trunk.

18:28.100 --> 18:29.400
You think so?

18:29.560 --> 18:31.690
Yeah, it gave me the shivers, too.

18:31.860 --> 18:33.230
Right, let's get on with the singing.

18:33.940 --> 18:34.530
All right!

18:35.990 --> 18:37.490
A medium menu and a beer.

18:37.650 --> 18:39.070
Same, but without onions.

18:39.280 --> 18:40.030
Average too.

18:43.580 --> 18:44.790
You're all hoarse!

18:45.200 --> 18:48.040
You shouldn't have told me to sing at the top of my voice.

18:48.370 --> 18:51.790
All right, but at this point, it's an achievement!

18:52.210 --> 18:53.500
Don't touch me.

18:53.670 --> 18:55.210
"Thank… you… very… much."

18:57.260 --> 19:01.430
Well, your voice should come back tomorrow. Until then, save it.

19:01.590 --> 19:02.930
Are you a band?

19:04.260 --> 19:05.810
The guitar case tickled me.

19:08.230 --> 19:09.810
Come and see us, if you like.

19:11.350 --> 19:12.650
We'd love to.

19:14.730 --> 19:15.820
SHIN-KAWASAKI (TENTATIVE)

19:14.900 --> 19:15.820
You know everything.

19:16.610 --> 19:17.360
What do you mean?

19:17.650 --> 19:20.740
Well, we could show them our project.

19:22.120 --> 19:23.530
Let's take the temperature.

19:24.240 --> 19:25.620
Thank you and have a nice evening.

19:25.830 --> 19:27.370
Well, I've got to run.

19:28.160 --> 19:28.910
Away where?

19:29.080 --> 19:29.830
To work.

19:30.540 --> 19:31.080
See ya.

19:37.170 --> 19:39.720
She invited us again, after all.

19:40.220 --> 19:42.180
She paid for the rent and the food.

19:46.600 --> 19:48.520
What's she looking at?

19:49.350 --> 19:51.640
Her old bandmates.

19:53.100 --> 19:53.770
Behold.

19:57.860 --> 20:01.280
<i>Time for the very first performance of a young band!</i>

20:02.070 --> 20:05.530
<i>A trio straight from Kawasaki!</i>

20:06.530 --> 20:08.540
<i>Make some noise for…</i>

20:12.580 --> 20:14.460
<i>"Shin-Kawasaki"?</i>

20:14.790 --> 20:17.500
<i>We'll have to discuss the name again.</i>

20:17.670 --> 20:19.960
<i>It's only temporary, I assure you.</i>

20:20.260 --> 20:21.840
<i>Sorry we're late.</i>

20:25.100 --> 20:26.430
<i>Just a minute.</i>

20:27.220 --> 20:29.430
<i>Don't tell me that's your stage outfit.</i>

20:29.890 --> 20:31.100
<i>What's wrong with it?</i>

20:31.390 --> 20:34.100
<i>You've got to get naked, you know.</i>

20:35.310 --> 20:36.230
<i>Go change.</i>

20:42.490 --> 20:44.990
<i>Testing. Announcement. Announcement to come.</i>

20:45.240 --> 20:48.240
<i>You needed an outfit you hate.</i>

20:48.740 --> 20:50.330
<i>Don't let it go to your head.</i>

20:50.500 --> 20:54.250
<i>You've got to let your emotions flow.</i>

20:54.790 --> 20:57.170
<i>Don't worry, you're not alone.</i>

20:57.670 --> 20:59.750
<i>You're shy, but stubborn.</i>

21:00.130 --> 21:02.010
<i>Cowardly but self-assured.</i>

21:02.510 --> 21:05.260
<i>A real walking paradox.</i>

21:05.590 --> 21:06.930
Great, thanks for nothing!

21:08.010 --> 21:10.520
Come on, Nina! We're next!

21:11.730 --> 21:15.020
<i>You've built up so much anger and energy.</i>

21:15.350 --> 21:16.190
<i>And this…</i>

21:17.190 --> 21:19.110
<i>is what we call rock.</i>

21:21.860 --> 21:22.740
Rock?

21:25.570 --> 21:27.990
Nina Iseri: Rina Momoka Kawaragi: Yûri

21:33.040 --> 21:36.420
<i>Nobody knows you. Nobody cares about you.</i>

21:37.130 --> 21:39.500
<i>But that's what makes it so exhilarating.</i>

21:55.230 --> 21:58.560
Translation & Subtitling: JSICMF Proofreading: Sarah Courchay

21:58.860 --> 22:01.320
You're rock'n'roll, Nina.

22:05.740 --> 22:07.490
<i>If nothing changes no matter how long you wait</i>

22:07.660 --> 22:10.870
<i>Then I see no common ground</i>

22:11.030 --> 22:15.710
<i>Blame is never enough to heal the wounds</i>

22:15.870 --> 22:18.460
<i>I want to say goodbye to these long days</i>

22:18.630 --> 22:20.790
<i>That I spent curled up</i>

22:21.090 --> 22:25.340
<i>It's not like I believe in some deity</i>

22:25.510 --> 22:30.350
<i>- Shut up
- Shut up</i>

22:30.640 --> 22:35.980
<i>- Leave me
- Leave me</i>

22:36.140 --> 22:38.560
<i>A stranger singing her heart out</i>

22:38.730 --> 22:41.020
<i>Promises me that nothing is an end in itself</i>

22:41.190 --> 22:45.030
<i>Perhaps these banalities In some hearts have resounded</i>

22:45.440 --> 22:47.070
<i>I ignore it</i>

22:47.240 --> 22:48.410
<i>I see</i>

22:48.570 --> 22:49.530
<i>I see</i>

22:49.700 --> 22:50.870
<i>I've forgotten</i>

22:51.030 --> 22:52.030
<i>I'm tired</i>

22:52.200 --> 22:53.330
<i>I want to break everything</i>

22:53.490 --> 22:55.330
<i>My courage has gone</i>

22:55.500 --> 23:00.960
<i>Please, someone give me a reason to exist</i>

23:01.130 --> 23:05.170
<i>I can't count the number of replacements</i>

23:05.420 --> 23:10.550
<i>It's easy to order me to be myself</i>

23:10.720 --> 23:13.470
<i>These words sound like a stage production</i>

23:13.640 --> 23:16.180
<i>Dreaming to see reality catch up</i>

23:16.350 --> 23:18.640
<i>Is there anyone?</i>

23:37.910 --> 23:40.670
<i>It's just crazy…</i>

23:42.210 --> 23:43.210
<i>That's rock.</i>

23:46.090 --> 23:46.800
I'M LEAVING THE BAND, SORRY!

23:47.630 --> 23:49.470
<i>Next: "Between Gratitude and Surprise".</i>
